gt9(){return"Exercise volume (total)"},
gt8(){return"Next to the progress (chart) button under the sets: total tonnage for this exercise\u2014the sum of weight \xd7 reps for every set that has both values. Updates live as you add or edit sets."},
gp9(){return"Personal progress"},
gtt(){return"One table of every movement from saved workouts: best set, estimated 1RM, and max volume. Search to find a name. Star favorites; tap the small chip under the name to tag a muscle group; the red X removes the name from suggestions and this table (saved workouts stay). Open it from your training menu or a client profile."},
gud(){return"Saving"},
gtf(){return"Finish workout"},
gte(){return"Confirms and writes the session to history. If you leave earlier, you can save, discard, or stay. A draft is also kept automatically if the app is interrupted."},
gu3(){return"Cardio & intensity"},
grU(){return"Cardio"},
grT(){return"Tracks time and intensity for cardio (distance is not entered). Helps you keep pace and monitor effort."},
gti(){return"Intensity"},
gth(){return"Use the effort scale to gauge how hard the workout felt. That is the key to progress without overtraining."},
guf(){return"Stopwatch (your assistant)"},
guy(){return"Why use it?"},
gux(){return"To control rest between sets. Short rest \u2014 higher density; long rest \u2014 more strength for heavy weight."},
gun(){return"How does it work?"},
gum(){return"Center: time, Play/Pause, and Reset. Left and right: quick presets (below). In plain stopwatch mode time runs up with centiseconds. The timer stays pinned in the header while you scroll."},
guq(){return"Left: intervals"},
guo(){return"1/1 \u2014 60 s work, 60 s rest. 4/4 \u2014 4 minutes work and 4 minutes rest each round. 20/10 \u2014 Tabata-style: 20 s on, 10 s off. After you pick one, the timer loops work and rest until you pause or reset. Red tint means work; blue means rest."},
guu(){return"Right: rest countdown"},
gut(){return"+1m, +2m, and +5m start or extend a normal minute countdown. If an interval loop was running, it switches to this countdown. If a countdown is already running, the minutes are added to the time left. Handy for rest between sets."},
gus(){return"Progress bar"},
gur(){return"During countdown and interval modes, a bar under the time shows how much of the current phase remains."},
guw(){return"Sound & haptics"},
guv(){return"At 3, 2, and 1 seconds left in a phase, a short in-app sound and light haptic play. When the phase ends or work/rest switches, a stronger cue and haptic follow. Sounds are minimal bundled clips\u2014no microphone, no notification permission; media/system volume still affects loudness."},
gu9(){return"History & data"},
gtn(){return"History / statistics"},
gtm(){return"In calendar/history each workout shows total tonnage. Workout volume is one of the best indicators of hypertrophy: the more quality volume you accumulate, the more muscle you can build."},
gtq(){return"Import / export"},
gtp(){return"Back up or transfer your data using JSON export and import in the statistics dialog. Backups include workout history, your exercise list, favorites, and muscle-group tags. Coach backups are separate from personal history. A coach can also import an athlete's history as a new client without mixing exercise names."},
